read_stream.c: no pointer arithmetic on a NULL per-buffer-data pointer (intcap plan, Phase D).

get_per_buffer_data() returns `(char *) stream->per_buffer_data + size * index` for
every stream, and read_stream_look_ahead calls it even when the stream has no
per-buffer data. Then the pointer is NULL and the size 0. On Capstone, arithmetic on
a null capability is a cincoffset on an untagged value, which traps (cause 24) even
when it adds 0. That was the next fault in --boot once buffer allocation worked, at
read_stream_look_ahead. Return NULL when there is no per-buffer data.

Applies after 0008, which touches the same file.

--- a/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/aio/read_stream.c
@@ -160,6 +160,12 @@
 static inline void *
 get_per_buffer_data(ReadStream *stream, int16 buffer_index)
 {
+	/*
+	 * capstone: a stream without per-buffer data has a NULL pointer here, and
+	 * arithmetic on a null capability traps (cause 24), even to add 0.
+	 */
+	if (stream->per_buffer_data == NULL)
+		return NULL;
 	return (char *) stream->per_buffer_data +
 		stream->per_buffer_data_size * buffer_index;
 }
